WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.726
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 9: City Places.

2
00:00:03.806 --> 00:00:11.179
In this unit you will learn the words for places
in a town — the shop, the market, the school,

3
00:00:11.259 --> 00:00:13.478
the hospital and the library.

4
00:00:13.558 --> 00:00:22.200
You will learn about the people who work in these places,
and the words that tell us where something is: near,

5
00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:23.468
far and next to.

6
00:00:23.548 --> 00:00:30.366
You will meet the traffic lights too, and
learn that red means stop and green means go.

7
00:00:30.446 --> 00:00:37.660
A town is full of helpful places and kind
people, and we all help to keep it clean and safe.

8
00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:44.321
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

9
00:00:44.401 --> 00:00:53.005
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name places
in a town (shop, market, school, hospital, library, park).

10
00:00:53.085 --> 00:00:58.518
You will also name some people who
help us (teacher, doctor, shopkeeper).

11
00:00:58.598 --> 00:01:04.937
You will also say where a place is using
position words (near, next to, here, there).

12
00:01:05.017 --> 00:01:07.732
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:01:07.812 --> 00:01:13.554
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
shop, market, school, hospital, library, park.

14
00:01:13.634 --> 00:01:18.680
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:22.666
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:22.746 --> 00:01:27.323
The reading sequence includes A Walk
Around Town and Talk about City Places.

17
00:01:27.403 --> 00:01:28.180
Read actively.

18
00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:32.408
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:32.488 --> 00:01:36.390
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:40.236
The first language focus is Say what is in your town.

21
00:01:40.316 --> 00:01:42.268
Name one place in your town.

22
00:01:42.348 --> 00:01:47.855
Say 'a' before most words, but 'an'
before a vowel sound: a shop, an airport.

23
00:01:47.935 --> 00:01:55.765
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

24
00:01:55.845 --> 00:01:59.798
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 - Listen and point.

25
00:01:59.878 --> 00:02:04.228
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

26
00:02:04.308 --> 00:02:07.599
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

27
00:02:07.679 --> 00:02:11.103
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

28
00:02:11.183 --> 00:02:12.689
You are ready to begin.

29
00:02:12.769 --> 00:02:19.515
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

30
00:02:19.595 --> 00:02:22.825
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

31
00:02:22.905 --> 00:02:30.478
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
